# Intentionally empty. Do not delete.
#
# `wrangler types` and `wrangler deploy` read the repository's .env, which holds the
# testnet keys and the Circle credentials. That is convenient for the scripts and
# unwanted for the Worker: it makes unrelated names appear as bindings, and Cloudflare
# rejects a name that is both a var and a secret, so a stray binding can block a real
# secret from ever being set.
#
# Passing this file with --env-file overrides that lookup, which is why it exists and
# why it is one comment and nothing else. See the package.json scripts:
#
#   pnpm site:types     wrangler types --env-file worker/empty.env
#   pnpm site:deploy    wrangler deploy --env-file worker/empty.env
